# Own-wording items of Deep Magic (2014 rules). Row shape as tghp_item.py: add(name, type, rarity, attune, text, **opts).
# The source lists Book of Eibon, Nameless Cults and Necronomicon twice. One row each, written from the later wording.
# Mundane alchemical goods (Alchemist's Ice, Hypodermic Arrow, Swarm Repellent, Tooth Capsule) are GEAR rows.
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

def add(name, typ, rar, att, text, **o):
    ITEMS.append((name, typ, rar, att, text, o))

ING = " **Ingredients.** "

# ---- Elixirs (the six great alkemancer potions)
add("Black Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A greasy black liquid. **Drunk or rubbed on flesh.** It acts as poison and the user takes 12d6 poison damage, or half as much with a successful DC 20 Constitution saving throw. **Smeared on a doorway or other portal.** It works as Forbiddance for one year. There is no password and it affects only Celestials and Fiends. The maker chooses at creation whether the damage is Radiant or Necrotic." + ING + "The heart of a marut, the powdered horn of a ki-rin, and a vial of black mud from the bottom of a lake where at least one Celestial or Fiend has bathed.")
add("Golden Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A thick, golden, syrupy liquid. The drinker stops aging for good and becomes immune to all natural and magical diseases and poisons. Violence and other harm can still kill the drinker, but time no longer threatens them." + ING + "A thimble of distilled sunlight, the breath of a solar, and hair from a venerable sage at least 100 years old.")
add("Iron Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A dark, grainy, foul-tasting liquid. The drinker gains permanent resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage and a damage threshold of 5. The drinker's Speed drops by 10 ft and they always have Disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws and Dexterity checks. Nothing can cancel or overcome that Disadvantage." + ING + "The core of an iron golem, a shard of purest adamantine, and the powdered teeth of a mountain giant.")
add("Jade Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A bright green, fizzing elixir. The drinker always has Advantage on Charisma checks when dealing with extraplanar creatures. When the drinker calls or conjures a Celestial, Elemental, Fey, or Fiend, it arrives with maximum hit points." + ING + "The tears of an invisible stalker, the claw of a pit fiend, and the tongue of a bard of at least 10th level.")
add("Pearl Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A silvery-white elixir whose effect depends on how it is used. All effects are permanent. **Drunk.** You breathe air and water equally well. **Rubbed on the feet.** You walk on water as if wearing a Ring of Water Walking. **Smeared on a boat hull.** The vessel gains a damage threshold of 20 against all environmental effects, and whoever pilots it has Advantage on ability checks tied to piloting." + ING + "The scale of a merfolk princess, a vial of pure elemental water, and the eye of a kraken.")
add("Ruby Elixir", "Potion", "Legendary", 0, "A vermilion elixir. It ends all magical and nonmagical diseases and poisons, all curses of 8th level or lower, and all Exhaustion. It also restores hit points like a superior healing potion. Poured over a corpse dead for no more than a year, it returns the creature to life as Resurrection does, even if the corpse could not normally be resurrected." + ING + "Purest cinnabar, the blood of a slain dragon of at least adult age, and the hearts of six celestial tigers, each willingly donated to the alkemancer.")

# ---- Other potions and alchemical magic
add("Brain Juice", "Potion", "Very Rare", 0, "A foul, murky, purple-gray liquid made from the liquefied brains of spellcasters such as aboleths. The drinker makes a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw. **Success.** You regain 1d6 + 4 expended spell slots. **Failure.** You suffer short-term madness for 1 day. If you drink several doses and fail three saves in a row, you gain a long-term madness for good and automatically fail every later save against brain juice.")
add("Potion, Pill Form", "Potion", "Unknown", 0, "Rarity varies by potion type. A potion pressed into a pill works exactly like the regular potion and keeps its color, but it has almost no weight and hides easily in a boot, pouch, hatband, or secret pocket. You swallow a pill as a Bonus Action. A pill costs five times as much as the normal potion.")
add("Oil of Defoliation", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, "A greasy brown oil made from crushed locust husks. One vial coats one weapon or up to five pieces of ammunition and takes 1 minute to apply. For the next hour, each hit with the coated item deals an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage to plants and plant creatures. You can also apply it directly to a willing, helpless, or immobile plant or plant creature, which takes 4d6 Necrotic damage. That is enough to kill most plants smaller than a large tree.")
add("Scalehide Cream", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "Rub this dull green cream on your skin as an action to grow thick olive-green scales for 1 hour. The scales give you a natural AC of 15 + your Constitution modifier. This AC does not combine with worn armor or a Dexterity bonus to AC. A jar holds 1d6 + 1 doses.")
add("Bubbling Retort", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, "A long, thin retort of smoky yellow glass with a carved brass stopper. As an action, unstopper it and pour in any liquid. It spews multicolored bubbles in a 20-foot radius for 1d4 + 1 rounds. Creatures in the area are Blinded and the area is Heavily Obscured to everyone except creatures with tremorsense. The liquid is used up with no harmful side effect. Popped bubbles make a wet smack and do nothing else.")

# ---- Alchemy gear and workshop items
add("Alembic of Unmaking", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, "A glass retort on a bronze tripod, joined by a bronze spout to a smaller glass vessel, with amethyst sparks sometimes flickering in the glass. Put a magic item in the retort and light a fire beneath it to dissolve the item and drain its magic into the smaller vessel. Artifacts, legendary items, and anything larger than a shortsword or cloak cannot be dissolved. Ten minutes is enough to make most items nonmagical. One full hour turns the magic into arcanoplasm, a gray-purple dough that is safe to handle. Using arcanoplasm when you make a magic item cuts its cost by 10 percent per degree of rarity of the item distilled into it. The alembic handles one item per 24 hours.")
add("Girdle of Traveling Alchemy", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1, "A wide leather girdle with many sewn-in pouches and holsters holding empty beakers and vials. Once you attune to it, the containers fill with 2 flasks of Alchemist's Fire, 2 flasks of alchemist's ice, 2 vials of Acid, 2 jars of swarm repellent, 1 vial of assassin's blood poison, 1 potion of climbing, and 1 potion of healing. Everything refills each dawn while you wear the girdle. Any liquid moved to another container loses its properties before it is used.")
add("Anuraag's Crucible", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 0, "An enormous crucible of white clay engraved with mystical symbols chased in burnished copper and electrum. It holds one Huge, two Large, four Medium, or eight Small creatures. Heat it over an intense magical flame and each creature inside makes a DC 20 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, the body liquefies and the creature is Blinded, Deafened, and Paralyzed until the change ends. Its equipment does not dissolve. After 10 minutes, the creature becomes a new creature as if by Shapechange. If the process is interrupted, the creature dies, and Resurrection or similar magic restores its original form. The new form must also pass a DC 20 Wisdom saving throw or lose its memories and abilities to a blank, newborn mind. The new form is permanent, and only Wish or comparable magic restores the old one. Constructs, undead, and creatures that can change shape at will are immune. Roll a d20 for the result: 1 Cat, 2 Ape, 3 Camel, 4 Dire wolf, 5 Giant fly, 6 Giant lizard, 7 Giant toad, 8 Mastiff, 9 Tiger, 10 Basilisk, 11 Chimera, 12 Griffon, 13 Harpy, 14 Lamia, 15 Manticore, 16 Spirit naga, 17 Aboleth, 18 Gibbering mouther, 19 Gargoyle, 20 a new life form. **Destroying it.** If a Celestial and a Fiend, both of at least CR 15, willingly enter at the same time, the crucible bursts. All creatures within 60 ft take 20d6 Piercing damage, or half as much with a successful DC 15 Dexterity saving throw.")
add("Nithing Pole", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "A sturdy wooden staff 6 to 10 feet long, carved with runes naming one dishonored target, draped in horsehide, and topped with a horse skull. It is planted where the target will pass. The target must be named exactly, so a description such as the person who did some deed will not work. When the target comes within 60 ft, the pole casts Bestow Curse on them at a range of 60 ft, with a Wisdom save DC of 15. On a successful save, the pole casts it again every round until the target fails, leaves the range, or the pole is destroyed. Anyone other than its maker who tries to destroy or knock it down is hit by one Bestow Curse. The maker chooses the curse's effect at creation. The curse lasts 8 hours and needs no concentration. The pole turns nonmagical only after it curses its target, so a forgotten one can stay dangerous for centuries.")

# ---- Books of forbidden lore
add("Book of Eibon", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", 1, "A fragmentary black book said to come from forgotten Hyperborea. It holds these spells: Semblance of Dread, Ectoplasm, Animate Dead, Speak with Dead, Emanation of Yoth, Green Decay, Yellow Sign, Eldritch Communion, Create Undead, Gate, Harm, Astral Projection, and Void Rift, plus any others the GM chooses. If you are attuned, you can use it as a spellbook and an arcane focus. While holding it, you can cast a Necromancy spell written in it as a Bonus Action without a spell slot or Verbal and Somatic components. Once you do, you cannot do so again until the next dawn.", ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Nameless Cults", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", 1, "A dubious old book in heavy leather with iron hasps, full of forbidden secrets and blasphemy about nightmare cults and their nameless entities. It holds all the mythos spells of Deep Magic plus any others the GM chooses. When you make an Intelligence check to recall lore about evil or the occult, such as Great Old Ones, mythos creatures, or the cults that worship them, double your Proficiency Bonus on that check.")
add("Necronomicon", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 1, "A tome bound in humanoid skin with a leering ghoulish face on its cover. Reading it always has dire consequences. You must attune to it and then spend another 19 hours reading it. After that, you can add to and copy its contents, as long as the additions serve Chaos or Evil and build on the lore inside. No two copies are the same. A non-Evil creature that attunes makes a DC 18 Charisma saving throw or becomes Neutral Evil. Unseen evil forces pursue the owner. Once every three days while you are attuned, you have a 19 in 20 chance of meeting or being attacked by a mythos entity or occult foe of the GM's choice. If you die while attuned, a Great Old One claims your soul and you cannot be restored to life. **Random properties.** 2 minor beneficial, 1 major beneficial, 1 minor detrimental, and 2 major detrimental artifact properties. **Ability scores.** After the reading, your Intelligence rises by 2 (maximum 24) and your Wisdom falls by 2 (minimum 3). This happens only once. **Abstract formulae.** It holds all mythos and Void spells of Deep Magic, all standard Necromancy spells, and any others the GM chooses. **Eldritch magic.** Any spell slot you spend on a warlock or wizard spell counts as one level higher for the spell's effects. **Eldritch lore.** Double your Proficiency Bonus on Intelligence checks to recall lore about evil or the secrets of the multidimensional universe. **Eldritch guise.** You speak, read, and write Void Speech, and you can cast Semblance of Dread as a Bonus Action. **Voidmarked.** You gain a further flesh warp and an expanded indefinite madness. You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks against aberrations and on Charisma (Intimidation) checks against non-aberrations. **Thought control.** While holding the book, use an action to cast Dominate Monster (save DC 18). You cannot do so again until the next dawn. **Destroying it.** Torn pages find their way back as new authors or translators add to it. Rumor says it cannot be destroyed while a spawn of Azathoth exists. Casting it into the fire of a dying star wipes its pages and leaves it powerless for 6d6 + 6 years.")
add("Taergash's Exsanguinating Tome", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", 1, "Requires attunement by a wizard. A tome in a filthy cover that weeps warm blood. The gore never hides the spells for anyone who wants to read them. The book holds these spells. **Cantrip.** Blood Tide. **1st level.** Bane, False Life, Tasha's Hideous Laughter, Ray of Sickness, Stanch, Weapon of Blood. **2nd level.** Blood Armor, Blood Lure, Bloodshot, Caustic Blood, Vital Mark. **3rd level.** Animate Dead, Fear, Ray of Enfeeblement, Vampiric Touch. **4th level.** Blood and Steel, Phantasmal Killer. **5th level.** Cruor of Visions, Exsanguinating Cloud, Sanguine Horror.")

# ---- Ring wardens
add("Karrek's Bastion", "Wondrous Item", "Artifact", 1, "A sentient adamantine ring 3 inches across, set with gold-inlaid runes. It looks like a warden's link. **Weapon.** Attach it to a nonmagical weapon and the weapon becomes magical with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls and scores a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20. It deals an extra 1d10 Fire damage per hit, or 3d10 Fire damage to orcs, giants, goblins, and undead. **Random properties.** 2 minor beneficial, 1 minor detrimental, and 1 major detrimental artifact properties. **Unyielding spirit.** While you carry it, you have resistance to Necrotic damage, your hit point maximum cannot be reduced, and you cannot be Frightened. **Spells.** While it is on you, use an action to cast Death Ward, Heat Metal, or Stone Shape from it (save DC 18). Each spell can be cast once per day, and all return at dawn. **Sentience.** Lawful Good, Intelligence 14, Wisdom 16, Charisma 18. It has hearing and darkvision out to 120 ft and speaks telepathically with its wielder. It speaks, reads, and understands Common and Dwarvish. **Personality.** It exists to defend the ring wardens and their allies and to drive back the foes of the dwarves. It is stubborn, brave to a fault, and fond of wordplay. It urges you to put it on a maul above all weapons and grudgingly accepts any martial weapon. It clashes with you if you try a finesse or ranged weapon. It hates anyone who steals or misuses ring magic secrets and pushes you to hunt them down. **Destroying it.** Lay the ring on the first of the ring wardens' forges. One ring warden must slay another ring warden with the forge hammer. While the hammer is still warm with blood, it can unmake the ring on that forge.", fx={"res": ["Necrotic"], "condImm": ["Frightened"]}, ch=[3, "1", "dawn"])
SP["Karrek's Bastion"] = {"sp": [["Death Ward", 0], ["Heat Metal", 0], ["Stone Shape", 0]]}
add("Oathbound Ring", "Ring", "Legendary", 1, "A plain adamantine ring with dwarven runes of honor and fidelity inside the band. When you attune, you swear an oath to a person or an organization, such as the ring wardens. It must name a specific service to perform or action to avoid. While attuned, you resist Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from nonmagical attacks and you cannot willingly break your oath. A spell or effect that would force you to break it fails at once. If you swore secrecy, mind-reading magic finds nothing useful. When a creature directly tries to stop you from keeping your oath, you have Advantage on attack rolls, saving throws, and ability checks against it until it stops or dies. If you die wearing the ring, Speak with Dead and similar spells fail if the questions would break your oath. You cannot end attunement voluntarily and the ring cannot be removed. The ring is immune to Psychic, Poison, Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage, and has AC 20, a damage threshold of 30, and 50 hit points.")
add("Warden's Link", "Wondrous Item", "Unknown", 0, "A metal ring 3 inches across with dwarven runes, made by ring wardens to help allies in battle. Each one holds one enchantment meant for armor, a shield, or a weapon. Its rarity is one step above the enchantment it carries. For example, a link with the effects of Armor of Resistance or a +2 weapon is Very Rare. Attaching it to a nonmagical suit of armor, shield, or weapon of the right type takes 1 hour of work with suitable tools, usually leatherworker's or smith's tools, and can be done during a Short Rest. Removing it takes a similar process. While attached, the item is magical and gains the ring's effects. If the enchantment needs attunement, the person doing the work can attune during that same hour. Anyone else needs a separate hour. Rumors tell of links with legendary or artifact-level enchantments, but the truth is lost.")
_forge = "A magical furnace and anvil patterned on the original forges in the deep halls of the ring wardens. A warlord who champions the wardens may rarely receive one as a gift. A character proficient with smith's tools who makes weapons or armor of enough quality at the forge finds them imbued with magic. The forge lets you make magic weapons and armor without finding a formula. The best quality it can produce is %s. You supply the required gold and make progress as for crafting any magic item. If you do not meet the level requirement for the item's rarity, you can try a Wisdom check with smith's tools against DC 10 + 5 for every rarity level above Uncommon. On a success, the item is made. On a failure, the enchantment fails and the gold and time produce a nonmagical but likely high-quality item. Every item made here needs GM approval, and the GM may ask for extra components or materials."
add("Rare Molten Fire Forge", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _forge % "Uncommon")
add("Very Rare Molten Fire Forge", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _forge % "Rare")
add("Legendary Molten Fire Forge", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", 0, _forge % "Very Rare")

# ---- Mundane alchemical goods: name, cost gp, weight lb, type, text
GEAR += [
 ["Alchemist's Ice", 50, 1, "Alchemical", "A blue-white flask, cool to the touch, holding a volatile liquid that turns to ice in air. Poured on a surface, it makes a 5-foot patch of ice that works as regular ice for movement. You can throw it like a flask of Alchemist's Fire. On a hit it deals 1d8 Cold damage, and the target makes a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or has its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of your next turn."],
 ["Hypodermic Arrow", 25, 0.05, "Ammunition", "An arrow with a syringe for a head. When it hits a creature it deals 1d4 Piercing damage plus the effect of whatever liquid the syringe injects, such as poison, acid, drugs, or potions. It always breaks on impact, hit or miss. It is sold empty, though ones found in hoards may be filled. Filling the syringe takes an action and can be done hours or days ahead."],
 ["Swarm Repellent", 40, 1, "Alchemical", "A slimy yellow paste smeared on exposed skin. A swarm of ants, beetles, biting flies, wasps, or similar insects that enters your space must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be unable to attack you. A repelled swarm repeats the save at the start of its next turn, and most swarms look for easier prey. One jar protects two Medium or four Small creatures. Applying it takes 1 minute. It works for 1 hour or until you are immersed in water."],
 ["Tooth Capsule", 100, 0, "Alchemical", "A false tooth, or a cap over a real one, holding one dose of a potion in pill form. The pill cannot be swapped out. To use it, bite down as a Bonus Action and make a DC 10 Strength check. On a success, the capsule breaks and you can swallow, hold, or spit out the pill. Spotting a tooth capsule in another creature's mouth needs a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Medicine) check, and the creature must be Restrained, Unconscious, Paralyzed, or cooperative. Spies and fanatics often load them with poison. The price is 100 gp plus the cost of the loaded potion, and some places outlaw harmful contents, which raises black market prices."],
]
